1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,212
There were fourteen monitors, and every one of them turned red at once.

2
00:00:06,212 --> 00:00:11,548
National Security Adviser Brian Collins did not get up from his chair.

3
00:00:11,548 --> 00:00:17,265
The most dangerous moment in a war isn't when everyone jumps to their feet.

4
00:00:17,265 --> 00:00:18,941
It's when no one does.

5
00:00:18,941 --> 00:00:21,076
Confusion makes people move.

6
00:00:21,076 --> 00:00:23,058
Panic makes them go still.

7
00:00:23,058 --> 00:00:26,651
“NATO's out, sir. Japan too. Korea. Australia.”

8
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:28,792
His aide kept his voice low.

9
00:00:28,792 --> 00:00:30,627
Collins didn't even nod.

10
00:00:30,627 --> 00:00:32,997
An alliance was never a person.

11
00:00:32,997 --> 00:00:38,885
An alliance was a system, and systems always flow toward their own interests.

12
00:00:38,885 --> 00:00:41,943
A war you start alone, you finish alone.

